  "corrections": [
    "emb-serial-buses.md: Correct protocol accounting.",
    "emb-control-to-audio.md: A block counter is not proof that a specific publication was adopted.",
    "emb-control-to-audio.md: Overflow can lose note offs and requires recovery.",
    "emb-control-to-audio.md: Account for running status and one-byte events.",
    "emb-control-to-audio.md: A polled final state does not necessarily stick, but does lose transient events.",
    "emb-control-to-audio.md: Bound event work even if producer runs concurrently.",
    "emb-control-to-audio.questions.json: Atomics are not automatically lock-free.",
    "emb-control-to-audio.questions.json: Atomic variable does not make arbitrary expressions atomic or relaxed operations order payloads.",
    "emb-control-to-audio.questions.json: Publication ordering is not lifetime/reuse protection.",
    "emb-control-to-audio.questions.json: Correct throughput bound and safe overflow response.",
    "emb-control-to-audio.questions.json: Fix unsafe acknowledgement-counter example.",
    "emb-adc-knobs.questions.json: Original minimum claim wrong: one mux plus direct ADCs suffices for 16.",
    "emb-adc-knobs.md: A/B taper codes are not universal.",
    "emb-gpio-buttons.md: Nominal arithmetic is not worst-case component qualification.",
    "emb-codecs-i2s.md: Audio codecs need not be stereo.",
    "emb-mcu-firmware.md: Bare-metal properties are not universal MCU properties.",
    "emb-mcu-firmware.md: Linker region size is not total chip capacity.",
    "emb-mcu-firmware.md: Bootloader definition does not imply immutable memory.",
    "emb-platform-comparison.md: Explicitly identify unavailable project-specific content rather than imply verified compatibility/performance.",
    "emb-gpio-buttons.questions.json: Qualify nominal GPIO current calculation.",
    "emb-serial-buses.md: Remove unsupported most-common claim; hardware must follow actual timing mode.",
    "retrofit: glossary pcm3060 said '24-bit, 96 kHz' codec; TI lists ADC up to 96 kHz and DAC up to 192 kHz. Now states both.",
    "retrofit: glossary switch-bounce example said 'across 16 switches, with one outlier at 157 ms'; Ganssle tested 18 with two outliers excluded. Now matches Ganssle and the lesson.",
    "retrofit: emb-adc-knobs moving-average lag 'about M/2 readings, about 4 ms for M=8 at 1 kHz'; a causal M-point average lags (M−1)/2 readings: now 3.5 readings, 3.5 ms.",
    "retrofit: question formula blocks in emb-adc-knobs q10, emb-realtime-audio q7 and emb-serial-buses q11 used English words as symbols (up/down, typical/outlier, start/stop/D4/D5); replaced with f_up, p_up, load_typ, d_0 … d_9.",
    "retrofit: glossary aliases capturing ordinary English or other meanings removed (timer(s), bounce(s)/bouncing/bouncy, poll(s)/polled, stepping, spinning/spins, tolerances, lockout, boots, standard value(s), transient(s), ripple, settling, breakout(s), loopback, parity, full scan, acknowledge, maximum/max load, worst-case time, reordering/reordered, fragmentation/fragmented, tearing, tightly coupled, secure mode, overrun forms, round-trip latency, real-time/real time/realtime, atomic/atomically, hoist/hoisting, current limit(s), note on/off, control change, wrong address, leakage, linking, taper).",
    "retrofit: alias 'FS' (frame sync) removed: the same lesson uses FS as the full-scale symbol in a formula.",
    "retrofit: alias 'Daisy' removed: it captured 'daisy chain(s)' in synth/03 and synth/05.",
    "retrofit: terms 'Ringing' and 'Current loop' renamed to 'Ringing (signal edges)' and 'Current loop (signalling)' so they no longer capture tinnitus/room-mode 'ringing' (synth/06) or 'the current loop' in other subjects.",
    "retrofit: glossary definitions generalised where the same word has another meaning elsewhere in the app: flash memory, push-pull, analogue multiplexer, linear mapping, block size, jitter, debouncing, end-to-end latency.",
    "retrofit: glossary secure-mode definition cited the bootloader-chip page for a claim from the code-security page; now quotes PJRC's code-security page (JTAG cannot access internal memory in secure mode)."
  ],
